// @error a lambda returning an empty `[]` cannot build the string[] result its annotation asks for
// @error a lambda returning an empty `[]` cannot build the i32[][] result its annotation asks for
// A VERDICT PIN, not a log pin: there is no correct run for a `@log` to compare against.
// Un-floored, this program emitted a module whose lambda's `$fnsig` result was interned off the
// empty literal's element HOLE while the value call cast the funcref to the annotation's — the
// module builds and then dies with `wasm trap: indirect call type mismatch` for the nested-array
// element, and fails to validate at all (`type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found (ref
// $type)`) for the string element. Neither outcome is a value, so neither can be pinned as one.
//
// MASTER'S FAILURE MODE FOR THIS FILE IS "THE COMPILER DIED" — worth stating, because it is not
// the usual shape of a red fixture, and it is why the message pinned here could not have been
// observed before. On master `vl check` on this file exits 1 having printed a wasm backtrace
// through `vl-compiler.wasm` and `wasm trap: out of bounds array access`: no diagnostic at all,
// so the `@error` directives above match nothing and the case is red.
//
// WHAT IS UNSUPPORTED, precisely. `TyArray.aElem` is `-1` for an empty `[]` whose element type
// is not yet known — the absence of a rep, not a narrower rep — and the lambda
// contextual-return ladder adopts the annotation per ELEMENT REP: `i64`/`f64`/`f32` through
// `scalarLeafListRetName`, a struct element through `structElemListRetName`, a litunion element
// through `litUnionElemListRetName`. `i32` and `boolean` need no arm because they share the one
// i32-list backing, and the SAME note excluded `string[]` on the grounds that it
// "self-classifies identically to the annotation" — which is true of a NON-EMPTY literal and
// false of an empty one. So `string[]` and a nested `T[][]` reach emit unpinned, and this is the
// loud floor for them. The workaround the message names (a NAMED function with the same return
// annotation) lowers all of them today.
//
// The legs:
//   L1 a `string[]` element — the ref-list backing.
//   L2 a nested `i32[][]` element — the other backing with no adopt arm.
// The EXEMPT reps are pinned as passing programs in
// `tests/cases/arrays/lambda-empty-array-literal-return.vl`, so a floor that widened to catch
// them would redden that file rather than this one.

function main() {
  const fs: () => string[] = () => {
    return []
  }
  print(fs().length)
  const fn: () => i32[][] = () => {
    return []
  }
  print(fn().length)
}
main()
